{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-c3eb08b49c01a75a0ace","statement":"Suppose there is a lax symmetric monoidal functor\n\n\\[\n\\der: \\bfC^{\\op}\\to \\lincat_\\La.\n\\]\n\nWe regard it as a sheaf theory $\\corr(\\bfC)_{\\iso;\\all}\\to\\lincat_\\La$.\n\n- Let $\\mathrm{L}\\subset \\mathrm{HL}$ be a weakly stable class. I.e. morphisms in $\\mathrm{L}$ satisfy <<ref:assumptions.base.change.sheaf.theory.HL>>. Then $\\der$ extends uniquely to a sheaf theory\n\n\\[\n\\der^{\\mathrm{L}}: \\corr(\\bfC)_{\\mathrm{L};\\all}\\to \\lincat_\\La,\n\\]\n\nsuch that $g\\horizl=\\der(g)$ and $f\\vertl=\\der(f)^L$ for $f\\in \\mathrm{L}$.\n\n- Dually, let $\\mathrm{R}\\subset \\mathrm{HR}$ be a weakly stable class. I.e. morphisms in $\\mathrm{L}$ satisfy <<ref:assumptions.base.change.sheaf.theory.H>>. Then $\\der$ extends to a sheaf theory $\\der^{\\mathrm{R}}: \\corr(\\bfC)_{\\mathrm{R};\\all}\\to \\lincat_\\La$.\n\n- Now let $\\mathrm{I}\\subset \\mathrm{L}$ and $\\mathrm{P}\\subset \\mathrm{R}$ be two strongly stable classes of morphisms, and let $\\verti$ be a weakly stable class of morphisms containing both $\\mathrm{I}$ and $\\mathrm{P}$. Suppose\n\n- for every Cartesian diagram <<ref:eq:base-change-diagram-app>> with $f\\in \\mathrm{I}$ and $g\\in \\mathrm{P}$, $\\der^L(f)\\circ \\der(g')^R\\to \\der(g)^R\\circ \\der(f')^L$ is an isomorphism.\n\n- every $f\\in \\mathrm{I}\\cap \\mathrm{P}$ is $n$-truncated from some $n\\geq -2$ (which may depend on $f$);\n\n- every $f\\in \\verti$ admits a decomposition $f=f_{\\mathrm{P}}\\circ f_{\\mathrm{I}}$ with $f_{\\mathrm{I}}\\in \\mathrm{I}$ and $f_{\\mathrm{P}}\\in \\mathrm{P}$;\n\nThen there is a sheaf theory $\\der\\colon \\corr(\\bfC)_{\\verti;\\all}\\to \\lincat_\\La$ that extends $\\der^{\\mathrm{L}}|_{\\corr(\\bfC)_{\\mathrm{I};\\all}}$ and $\\der^{\\mathrm{R}}|_{\\corr(\\bfC)_{\\mathrm{P};\\all}}$.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"3d6acdebbb15af51a7157faf471648239358a85753c5f1b4338